FINDINGS #C967 054478a (Security 11-11), diffed against its parent 65575d2.
F1 (must fix): scripts/board-land.mjs runs from ~/.flight-board/current, and every release moves that link (board-release.mjs runs current.mjs). board-land.mjs is not in RELEASE_ENTRIES (or OWNER_ENTRIES), so a signed commit that changes it is landed and then governs the next landing with no owner install: it could drop the hold check, or push without the release tool. That breaks Security B (a release can't loosen the next one). Fix: add scripts/board-land.mjs to RELEASE_ENTRIES (its import closure follows), and the release test's owned list, with a test that a commit changing board-land.mjs is refused.
LOW1: landPlan drops a Board-Id that fails CARD_ID silently, so a tip carrying a valid card and a malformed one is judged on the valid one only. Treat any malformed id as unknown (wait).
Otherwise sound: notes are read from the first line on the exact tip; the release tool still checks every commit, the trailers, the fast-forward and the pins; a stale, missing or silent holds file lands nothing; the job never forces or touches a branch, note or hold; argv only (no shell).
